/* DISCOVERY / derivation: the GENERAL orthogonal-to-control regret TRANSFER theorem -- the general form
   of result 0 (which only stated the p=1 -> O(eps^2) and p=2 -> O(eps^4) instances). Claim: if the
   causal-effect estimator has error of order delta^p in the nuisance error delta (p = 1 plug-in, p = 2
   Neyman-orthogonal/DML, and higher p for higher-order-orthogonal estimators), then the
   certainty-equivalence control regret is of order delta^(2*p): the control map DOUBLES the estimator's
   order. This is a composition theorem, not an arithmetic coincidence -- it holds for every p because
   control regret is quadratic in the ACTION error and the optimal action is smooth in the effect. NB:
   we use the EXACT regret map R = (b^2+rr)*(u*(bhat)-u*(b))^2, not the local approximation C*(bhat-b)^2.
   Maxima is the source of truth. */
display2d : false$

us(bb) := bb*xt/(bb^2 + rr)$   /* optimal action, smooth in the effect b */

/* EXACT certainty-equivalence regret (completing the square, causal_mpc.mac): quadratic in the ACTION
   error u*(bhat)-u*(b), NOT a local linearisation in bhat-b. */
Rexact : (b^2 + rr)*(us(bhat) - us(b))^2$
print("EXACT regret R(bhat) = (b^2+rr)*(u*(bhat) - u*(b))^2  (not the local C*(bhat-b)^2)")$

/* transfer: u* is Lipschitz in b near b (derivative du_star/db bounded), so the action error is
   first-order in the effect error, |u*(bhat)-u*(b)| <= Lip*|bhat-b| + O((bhat-b)^2). */
dus : ratsimp(diff(us(b), b))$
print("du*/db =", dus, " = xt*(rr-b^2)/(b^2+rr)^2  (Lipschitz constant of the action transfer)")$
print("=> |u*(bhat)-u*(b)| = O(|bhat-b|), so R = O((bhat-b)^2) : regret quadratic in the EFFECT error")$

/* ORDER DOUBLING: if the estimator error is bhat - b = O(delta^p), then (bhat-b)^2 = O(delta^(2p)),
   hence R = O(delta^(2p)). The regret order is 2*p for every estimator order p. */
print("if bhat-b = O(delta^p) then (bhat-b)^2 = O(delta^(2p)) => R = O(delta^(2p)) : order DOUBLES")$
for p:1 thru 4 do print("  p =", p, " (estimator O(delta^", p, ")) -> regret O(delta^", 2*p, ")")$

/* instances recovering result 0: p=1 (plug-in) -> O(delta^2) ; p=2 (Neyman-orthogonal DML) -> O(delta^4).
   the general theorem SUBSUMES both and extends to higher-order-orthogonal estimators (p>=3). */
print("instances: p=1 plug-in -> O(delta^2) ; p=2 orthogonal/DML -> O(delta^4) ; general p -> O(delta^2p)")$

/* the doubling identity used in the Rocq proof: (delta^p)^2 = delta^(2*p) (pow_mult), composed with the
   quadratic regret bound R <= (b^2+rr)*Lip^2*(bhat-b)^2. */
print("Rocq core: (delta^p)^2 = delta^(2p) [pow_mult] composed with R <= K*(bhat-b)^2 [quadratic map]")$
